1
00:00:25,793 --> 00:00:27,992
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,336 --> 00:00:38,169
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,316 --> 00:00:51,316
♪ ♪

4
00:01:16,143 --> 00:01:18,076
♪ ♪

5
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:51,976
Sam, what is it?

6
00:01:52,046 --> 00:01:54,379
Thought I heard something.

7
00:01:57,484 --> 00:01:59,251
No, you're just
jumpy. Eh, maybe.

8
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:01,019
Here, take this.

9
00:02:01,088 --> 00:02:02,887
Go ahead.

10
00:02:04,525 --> 00:02:06,458
Ever hold a gun before?

11
00:02:06,527 --> 00:02:07,893
No.

12
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:08,894
.357

13
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:10,695
Magnum.

14
00:02:10,764 --> 00:02:11,963
Blow a hole in somebody

15
00:02:12,032 --> 00:02:14,032
big enough for a
cat to walk through.

16
00:02:18,205 --> 00:02:20,038
Or you can make me do

17
00:02:20,107 --> 00:02:21,139
whatever you want.

18
00:02:21,208 --> 00:02:22,740
Oh, you...

19
00:02:25,379 --> 00:02:27,824
No. You've got to get dressed.

20
00:02:27,848 --> 00:02:29,481
You're due in court.

21
00:02:31,752 --> 00:02:33,196
Mr. O'Malley,

22
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:34,898
is this one of the biggest
drug cases you've ever tried?

23
00:02:34,922 --> 00:02:36,299
What drug case?
There's no case here at all.

24
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:37,600
What about Rinaldi's
testimony today?

25
00:02:37,624 --> 00:02:38,924
Rinaldi?

26
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:41,259
The D.A.'s entire case
is based on the testimony

27
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:43,929
of a police informant,
a known felon

28
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:46,297
who'll say anything
to stay out of prison.

29
00:02:46,366 --> 00:02:48,078
Frankly, I'm amazed they're
even letting him testify,

30
00:02:48,102 --> 00:02:50,013
but I guess he's
all the D.A. has.

31
00:02:50,037 --> 00:02:51,037
Excuse me.

32
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,018
How long do you
expect this case to take?

33
00:02:55,042 --> 00:02:57,442
Mr. Rinaldi, you
testified yesterday

34
00:02:57,511 --> 00:02:59,611
you were present at Steven's Bar

35
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:03,014
on the night of August 22, 1989.

36
00:03:03,083 --> 00:03:06,017
And at that time, you
overheard my client

37
00:03:06,086 --> 00:03:09,387
buy $11 million worth of
cocaine from a Mr. Pedro Cruz.

38
00:03:09,456 --> 00:03:10,389
Is that correct?

39
00:03:10,457 --> 00:03:11,390
Yes, it is.

40
00:03:11,458 --> 00:03:12,657
And isn't it also true

41
00:03:12,726 --> 00:03:14,159
that four months ago,

42
00:03:14,228 --> 00:03:17,129
you were arrested for
possession of cocaine?

43
00:03:17,197 --> 00:03:18,496
Yes.

44
00:03:18,565 --> 00:03:22,000
Yes, and at that time,
you offered to testify

45
00:03:22,069 --> 00:03:25,003
against my client, Mr. Sam
Chandler, in exchange

46
00:03:25,072 --> 00:03:27,005
for immunity from prosecution.

47
00:03:27,074 --> 00:03:28,606
That doesn't change the facts.

48
00:03:28,675 --> 00:03:29,608
Oh, the facts.

49
00:03:29,676 --> 00:03:30,742
The facts.

50
00:03:30,810 --> 00:03:32,322
We'll get to the
facts in a minute.

51
00:03:32,346 --> 00:03:34,746
Were you or were you
not granted immunity?

52
00:03:34,815 --> 00:03:35,815
Yes, I was.

53
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:38,683
Yes, you were. Now, the facts.

54
00:03:38,752 --> 00:03:43,488
The night of August
22, 1989, you say

55
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:45,677
you went to Steven's
Bar with Mr. Chandler.

56
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:48,393
And when you overheard
this conversation,

57
00:03:48,462 --> 00:03:50,295
where exactly were you sitting?

58
00:03:50,363 --> 00:03:51,295
At the bar.

59
00:03:51,365 --> 00:03:53,965
You, Mr. Chandler and Mr. Cruz

60
00:03:54,034 --> 00:03:55,099
were sitting at the bar?

61
00:03:55,168 --> 00:03:56,379
No, they were at a table.

62
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:58,837
Oh, they were at a table,
and you were at the bar.

63
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:00,784
So, in other words, you
weren't sitting with them

64
00:04:00,808 --> 00:04:01,884
when you overheard
this conversation?

65
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:03,308
That's right.

66
00:04:03,377 --> 00:04:06,911
Now, Steven's is sort of a
small singles bar, isn't it?

67
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:08,024
Yeah.

68
00:04:08,048 --> 00:04:09,548
Yeah. And it was a Friday night,

69
00:04:09,616 --> 00:04:11,194
so the place must
have been jammed.

70
00:04:11,218 --> 00:04:12,150
Yeah.

71
00:04:12,219 --> 00:04:13,697
What would you say,
there were about 60,

72
00:04:13,721 --> 00:04:15,131
70 people there? Yeah.

73
00:04:15,155 --> 00:04:16,499
About the same number
as in this courtroom? Yeah.

74
00:04:16,523 --> 00:04:18,290
Yeah, something like that.

75
00:04:18,359 --> 00:04:19,869
Your Honor, with
the court's indulgence,

76
00:04:19,893 --> 00:04:22,861
I would like to try and
reconstruct the circumstances

77
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:24,996
at Steven's Bar on
the night in question.

78
00:04:25,065 --> 00:04:26,431
Objection, Your
Honor. Relevance.

79
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,777
Overruled.

80
00:04:27,801 --> 00:04:31,536
Given the potential damage
of this witness's testimony,

81
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,816
I'm going to allow
Mr. O'Malley to continue.

82
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:36,240
Thank you, Your Honor.

83
00:04:36,309 --> 00:04:38,677
All right, ladies and gentlemen,
uh, we need your help.

84
00:04:38,745 --> 00:04:39,977
We need you to pretend

85
00:04:40,047 --> 00:04:43,115
that you're at a
bar, it's Friday night,

86
00:04:43,183 --> 00:04:44,783
you're out with some friends,

87
00:04:44,851 --> 00:04:46,785
uh, having a couple of drinks,

88
00:04:46,853 --> 00:04:48,753
talking, laughing, having

89
00:04:48,822 --> 00:04:50,989
a good time, okay?

90
00:04:51,058 --> 00:04:53,392
It's okay, folks,
you can do this.

91
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:54,559
You heard the judge.

92
00:04:54,628 --> 00:04:55,838
He said it was okay, right?

93
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:59,342
Uh-huh. Yeah, no.

94
00:04:59,366 --> 00:05:00,732
I said a good time.

95
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,233
A good time, yeah.

96
00:05:04,638 --> 00:05:05,715
Folks, come on.

97
00:05:05,739 --> 00:05:07,650
I've heard rowdier
groups at a funeral.

98
00:05:07,674 --> 00:05:08,885
Louder. Louder, everybody.

99
00:05:12,813 --> 00:05:15,781
Would you say this is
about the distance it was

100
00:05:15,849 --> 00:05:17,048
to, uh, Mr. Chandler?

101
00:05:17,117 --> 00:05:19,650
I-I don't... I can't
hear you. I...

102
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,064
You having a
problem, Mr. Rinaldi?

103
00:05:21,088 --> 00:05:22,020
I can't hear you.

104
00:05:22,089 --> 00:05:23,421
Folks!

105
00:05:23,490 --> 00:05:25,302
Quiet, please.

106
00:05:25,326 --> 00:05:27,859
Mr. Rinaldi can't hear me.

107
00:05:27,928 --> 00:05:30,406
And if you can't hear me now
in this courtroom, Mr. Rinaldi,

108
00:05:30,430 --> 00:05:31,730
how in the hell

109
00:05:31,798 --> 00:05:34,866
can you sit there and testify
under penalty of perjury

110
00:05:34,934 --> 00:05:36,713
that you could
overhear a conversation

111
00:05:36,737 --> 00:05:39,203
at a crowded singles
bar on a Friday night

112
00:05:39,273 --> 00:05:41,439
between my client and Mr. Cruz

113
00:05:41,508 --> 00:05:44,109
when you were sitting at a
bar halfway across the room?

114
00:05:44,177 --> 00:05:46,311
You know what I
think, Mr. Rinaldi?

115
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:49,080
You didn't hear one word
of that conversation, did you?

116
00:05:49,149 --> 00:05:50,848
Not one word.

117
00:05:50,917 --> 00:05:52,884
No further questions.

118
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:02,605
Has the jury reached a verdict?

119
00:06:02,629 --> 00:06:07,265
We find the defendant,
Samuel Chandler, not guilty.

120
00:06:07,334 --> 00:06:09,646
Thank you, ladies and
gentlemen of the jury.

121
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:11,580
This court stands adjourned.

122
00:06:12,673 --> 00:06:15,406
It's okay, Deputy.
That's my wife.

123
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:18,577
Congratulations, Mr. Chandler.

124
00:06:18,645 --> 00:06:19,578
She's something.

125
00:06:19,646 --> 00:06:21,324
Ah, you were
wonderful, my darling.

126
00:06:21,348 --> 00:06:23,481
It's good to have you back.

127
00:06:50,544 --> 00:06:51,476
Yes. All right.

128
00:06:51,545 --> 00:06:53,378
Hey, Sam. Hey, congratulations.

129
00:06:53,446 --> 00:06:55,814
I hear O'Malley was terrific.

130
00:06:55,883 --> 00:06:57,949
Quite a show, quite a show.

131
00:06:58,018 --> 00:06:59,050
Pour me a drink.

132
00:06:59,119 --> 00:07:00,785
Sure.

133
00:07:00,854 --> 00:07:03,021
I take it you all heard
from Jack Rinaldi.

134
00:07:03,090 --> 00:07:05,368
I'm not paying
him another penny.

135
00:07:05,392 --> 00:07:06,324
Relax, Bobby.

136
00:07:06,393 --> 00:07:08,360
Did you get a tape?

137
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:10,428
An excerpt. I think we
got to do something.

138
00:07:10,497 --> 00:07:11,429
You know,

139
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:14,131
I expect Bobby to
go off half-cocked,

140
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,734
but you, Al, too?

141
00:07:15,803 --> 00:07:18,703
I thought you were
smarter than that.

142
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:40,239
Just a minute.

143
00:07:42,496 --> 00:07:43,761
Yes?

144
00:07:48,201 --> 00:07:49,567
David.

145
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,207
What are you doing here?

146
00:07:56,276 --> 00:07:58,442
That's my line.

147
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:02,980
Dave, let's be calm about this.

148
00:08:03,050 --> 00:08:04,182
It's not serious.

149
00:08:04,251 --> 00:08:05,428
Where's Sam?

150
00:08:05,452 --> 00:08:06,918
I don't know.

151
00:08:06,986 --> 00:08:07,919
Where is he?

152
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:08,920
I don't know.

153
00:08:08,989 --> 00:08:10,600
Where is he?

154
00:08:10,624 --> 00:08:12,590
At Todd's Grill.

155
00:08:12,659 --> 00:08:14,292
<i>Sam, that tape</i>

156
00:08:14,361 --> 00:08:17,562
gets in the wrong hands, it
could mean life for all of us.

157
00:08:17,631 --> 00:08:20,097
That's not what Rinaldi
wants; he wants money.

158
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:22,066
A few bucks.

159
00:08:22,135 --> 00:08:23,467
The moment he turns that tape

160
00:08:23,537 --> 00:08:26,737
over to the police,
he's out of business.

161
00:08:26,806 --> 00:08:28,884
A million dollars is
more than a few bucks.

162
00:08:28,908 --> 00:08:30,308
You kill Rinaldi,

163
00:08:30,377 --> 00:08:32,322
the police are
gonna come after me.

164
00:08:32,346 --> 00:08:33,611
Take a vacation.

165
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:36,180
The Greek Isles are
beautiful this time of year.

166
00:08:37,984 --> 00:08:40,084
Perhaps I didn't
make myself clear.

167
00:08:42,155 --> 00:08:45,389
If I hear that Jack Rinaldi
slipped in the shower,

168
00:08:45,459 --> 00:08:49,927
or hung himself because he
was distraught or depressed,

169
00:08:49,996 --> 00:08:52,264
I'll know who killed him.

170
00:08:52,332 --> 00:08:53,998
You threatening me?

171
00:08:54,067 --> 00:08:57,035
I just came this close
to going to prison.

172
00:08:57,103 --> 00:08:58,269
That's close enough!

173
00:09:02,509 --> 00:09:03,441
David!

174
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:04,510
What are you doing here?

175
00:09:04,577 --> 00:09:05,588
Stay away from my wife,

176
00:09:05,612 --> 00:09:07,123
or I'll kill you! Cool it!

177
00:09:07,147 --> 00:09:08,658
I'll kill you, you
understand! Hold it! Hold it!

178
00:09:08,682 --> 00:09:11,116
I'll kill you. Come on, come on.

179
00:09:16,790 --> 00:09:18,723
Hello. Maintenance.

180
00:09:48,821 --> 00:09:50,755
♪ ♪

181
00:10:21,321 --> 00:10:23,188
Eh, boy.

182
00:10:23,256 --> 00:10:24,256
End of the ride.

183
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,657
This is your favorite spot, huh?

184
00:10:30,864 --> 00:10:32,630
What are you doing here?

185
00:10:52,519 --> 00:10:55,119
David, that was a
dumb thing to do.

186
00:10:55,188 --> 00:10:58,723
Punching out Sam Chandler
is like taking on Mike Tyson.

187
00:10:58,792 --> 00:11:00,257
It's really stupid.

188
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:01,537
Did anybody see you?

189
00:11:01,561 --> 00:11:05,363
Well, we were in the
back room at Todd's Grill.

190
00:11:05,432 --> 00:11:06,432
Jim Steinbach,

191
00:11:06,466 --> 00:11:08,967
Al Brackman and
Bobby Boyd were there.

192
00:11:09,035 --> 00:11:12,203
Do you know who
those fellas are?

193
00:11:12,272 --> 00:11:15,773
Ben, at one time or another,
I've represented all of them.

194
00:11:15,842 --> 00:11:19,243
Not for jaywalking, I'm sure.

195
00:11:19,312 --> 00:11:21,190
Not one of them ever
got convicted of a crime

196
00:11:21,214 --> 00:11:24,081
while I was representing
them, including Sam Chandler.

197
00:11:24,150 --> 00:11:25,083
Sam Chandler.

198
00:11:25,152 --> 00:11:28,620
Crook. Big dope dealer.

199
00:11:28,689 --> 00:11:30,088
Not according to the jury.

200
00:11:33,293 --> 00:11:35,960
One of his friends killed him.

201
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:38,329
With your gun. What
was your gun doing there?

202
00:11:38,398 --> 00:11:40,831
Well, they stole
it out of my office.

203
00:11:40,901 --> 00:11:42,767
Look, I already told the police,

204
00:11:42,835 --> 00:11:45,403
I can account for my actions
at the time of the murder.

205
00:11:45,471 --> 00:11:47,383
I was being hit up
for free legal advice

206
00:11:47,407 --> 00:11:49,941
by a bellman at the
hotel. There's no bellman

207
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:51,942
there that fits
your description.

208
00:11:52,012 --> 00:11:54,145
Oh, really? Well,
that's a surprise.

209
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:57,114
Come on. I'm being
framed, Ben. Obviously.

210
00:11:57,184 --> 00:11:59,284
Look, as soon as I get out here,

211
00:11:59,352 --> 00:12:02,186
I'll write you a check for the full
amount of your fee. I-I assume

212
00:12:02,255 --> 00:12:04,288
our-our fees are comparable.

213
00:12:04,357 --> 00:12:07,024
Well, what do you
get for a case like this?

214
00:12:07,094 --> 00:12:10,294
$125,000 plus expenses.

215
00:12:12,198 --> 00:12:14,365
Huh.

216
00:12:14,434 --> 00:12:17,268
Is there... is there a
problem with the figure?

217
00:12:17,337 --> 00:12:18,970
Oh, no, no.

218
00:12:19,039 --> 00:12:23,541
No, I-I usually get,
um, a little bit more.

219
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:40,369
Good morning,
Mr. O'Malley. They're all here.

220
00:12:40,393 --> 00:12:43,661
I thought you rented
small temporary quarters.

221
00:12:43,730 --> 00:12:45,062
I did.

222
00:12:45,131 --> 00:12:46,230
Come on.

223
00:12:51,204 --> 00:12:53,049
Morning. Morning. Good morning.

224
00:12:53,073 --> 00:12:55,006
I've had my staff
stay on here in Atlanta.

225
00:12:55,075 --> 00:12:57,675
We've put our heads together
and given the case some thought.

226
00:12:57,744 --> 00:13:00,712
Now, we already have files
on everyone who heard me

227
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:02,291
threaten Sam Chandler. David?

228
00:13:02,315 --> 00:13:04,126
I think we should put a
tail on each of them, though.

229
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:06,984
David? Now, the medical
examiner found that

230
00:13:07,053 --> 00:13:09,053
Sam's right index
finger was broken

231
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:10,889
just before he died. David!

232
00:13:10,957 --> 00:13:12,489
What?

233
00:13:12,559 --> 00:13:14,492
Um...

234
00:13:17,030 --> 00:13:21,098
Did you sign me on,
uh, to defend you?

235
00:13:23,436 --> 00:13:26,237
You want me to send them home?

236
00:13:26,305 --> 00:13:30,642
Well, we're both not
going to represent you...

237
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:34,311
People?

238
00:13:34,381 --> 00:13:35,980
Uh, that'll be it for today.

239
00:13:36,048 --> 00:13:38,583
We'll arrange
your transportation

240
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:40,618
back to New York first
thing in the morning.

241
00:13:40,687 --> 00:13:42,587
Thank you. Thank
you all for your work.

242
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:44,488
Can I at least, uh,
give you the files

243
00:13:44,558 --> 00:13:47,291
on Bobby Boyd, Jim
Steinbach and Al Brackman?

244
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:50,227
Fine.

245
00:13:50,296 --> 00:13:52,363
Here you go.

246
00:13:52,432 --> 00:13:54,231
Is, um...

247
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,000
Is your wife still in town?

248
00:13:56,069 --> 00:13:58,247
Yeah. She's at
the Wilton Towers.

249
00:13:58,271 --> 00:14:00,071
She won't talk to me.

250
00:14:00,139 --> 00:14:01,651
I don't think she'll
talk to you, either.

251
00:14:01,675 --> 00:14:04,241
Maybe not.

252
00:14:04,310 --> 00:14:06,288
What do you want me to do?

253
00:14:06,312 --> 00:14:09,613
Oh, go back to your hotel,
look at television, read...

254
00:14:09,683 --> 00:14:11,783
Ben, I'm a good investigator

255
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:13,529
and a damn good
attorney. You know that.

256
00:14:13,553 --> 00:14:16,654
Well, then, maybe you
should represent yourself.

257
00:14:16,722 --> 00:14:18,722
No.

258
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:21,259
Anything else?

259
00:14:21,327 --> 00:14:23,994
Well, yeah.

260
00:14:24,064 --> 00:14:29,033
Uh, most good lawyers
make lousy defendants.

261
00:14:29,102 --> 00:14:31,835
I'm sure I would,
too. We all have

262
00:14:31,905 --> 00:14:33,682
reputations.
You're a jet setter.

263
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:35,572
Hot tempered.

264
00:14:35,641 --> 00:14:37,474
Uh, two-fisted drinker.

265
