Hi. Oh... oh, are you all right?

538
00:30:43,442 --> 00:30:45,408
Let's get some ice on that.

539
00:30:48,747 --> 00:30:50,058
<i>He was looking</i>

540
00:30:50,082 --> 00:30:51,782
for her boyfriend, Jack Rinaldi.

541
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:53,183
Oh.

542
00:30:53,251 --> 00:30:54,317
David!

543
00:30:54,386 --> 00:30:55,830
Hi. The cleaning crew let me in.

544
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:57,699
What are you doing
looking through my stuff?

545
00:30:57,723 --> 00:30:59,367
Well, the preliminary
hearing is tomorrow, Ben.

546
00:30:59,391 --> 00:31:00,824
I want to see what you have.

547
00:31:00,893 --> 00:31:02,003
You got anything at all?

548
00:31:02,027 --> 00:31:03,827
You know Jack Rinaldi?
Yeah, I know him.

549
00:31:03,896 --> 00:31:06,508
He seems to be the
key to this case. No.

550
00:31:06,532 --> 00:31:08,810
He's totally unimportant.
And if that's all you have,

551
00:31:08,834 --> 00:31:11,179
we're going into court
tomorrow with nothing. David, I

552
00:31:11,203 --> 00:31:13,469
don't want you looking
through my stuff.

553
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:15,416
I've got other
cases with secrets

554
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:16,985
that have nothing
to do with you,

555
00:31:17,009 --> 00:31:18,854
and I don't want
you looking at them!

556
00:31:18,878 --> 00:31:21,077
I just wanted to
see what you've got.

557
00:31:22,781 --> 00:31:25,414
I... you work so
differently than I do, Ben.

558
00:31:25,484 --> 00:31:27,650
We're not going to
trial in the morning.

559
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:28,852
We've got time.

560
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:31,388
I know I work
differently from you.

561
00:31:31,457 --> 00:31:33,935
And I know that must make
you nervous. I guess I'd

562
00:31:33,959 --> 00:31:36,159
be nervous, too, if
I faced the prospect

563
00:31:36,227 --> 00:31:38,929
of going to prison
for the rest of my life.

564
00:31:38,997 --> 00:31:40,430
I can step aside.

565
00:31:40,499 --> 00:31:43,044
I can step aside, you
can get somebody else,

566
00:31:43,068 --> 00:31:45,701
or you can handle it yourself.

567
00:31:45,771 --> 00:31:48,672
But, like they say, a man
who represents himself

568
00:31:48,741 --> 00:31:50,574
has a fool for a lawyer.

569
00:31:50,643 --> 00:31:51,686
Here.

570
00:31:51,710 --> 00:31:53,822
Take the rest of
Conrad's popcorn,

571
00:31:53,846 --> 00:31:55,690
go home and think it over.

572
00:31:55,714 --> 00:31:57,392
But whatever you decide,

573
00:31:57,416 --> 00:31:59,616
you're not getting my fee back.

574
00:32:07,159 --> 00:32:08,858
Thank you.

575
00:32:17,102 --> 00:32:19,836
I want you to find Jack Rinaldi.

576
00:32:21,406 --> 00:32:23,239
And make him disappear.

577
00:32:32,417 --> 00:32:34,184
Keep me posted.

578
00:32:58,877 --> 00:33:01,022
♪ Won't you come
home, Bill Bailey? ♪

579
00:33:01,046 --> 00:33:02,679
♪ Won't you come home? ♪

580
00:33:02,748 --> 00:33:06,149
♪ She moaned the
whole night long ♪

581
00:33:06,218 --> 00:33:08,018
♪ I'll do the cookin', honey ♪

582
00:33:08,087 --> 00:33:09,853
♪ I'll pay the rent ♪

583
00:33:09,922 --> 00:33:13,190
♪ I know I done you wrong ♪

584
00:33:13,258 --> 00:33:15,225
♪ Remember that rainy evening ♪

585
00:33:15,293 --> 00:33:16,793
♪ I threw you out ♪

586
00:33:16,862 --> 00:33:20,263
♪ With nothing but
a fine-tooth comb? ♪

587
00:33:20,331 --> 00:33:22,265
♪ I know I'm to blame ♪

588
00:33:22,333 --> 00:33:24,167
♪ Ain't that a shame? ♪

589
00:33:24,236 --> 00:33:26,580
♪ Bill Bailey, won't you
please come home? ♪

590
00:33:26,604 --> 00:33:27,982
♪ Yeah! Yeah! ♪
Yeah.

591
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:30,051
♪ Bill Bailey, won't you
please come home? ♪

592
00:33:30,075 --> 00:33:31,719
Oh, yeah. Yeah.

593
00:33:31,743 --> 00:33:34,277
♪ Bill Bailey, won't you
please come home? ♪

594
00:33:35,681 --> 00:33:36,791
Oh. Yeah.

595
00:33:38,083 --> 00:33:40,195
That was good. All ready
for Biloxi, Mississippi.

596
00:33:40,219 --> 00:33:41,219
Close.

597
00:33:45,024 --> 00:33:47,324
You're my lawyer?

598
00:33:48,527 --> 00:33:50,827
Well, hell, I get
to have a little fun.

599
00:33:50,896 --> 00:33:52,529
Uh-huh.

600
00:33:52,598 --> 00:33:54,263
You want something?

601
00:33:54,332 --> 00:33:55,599
Chili's pretty good.

602
00:33:55,667 --> 00:33:56,667
Maybe later.

603
00:33:56,735 --> 00:33:57,901
So, what's so urgent?

604
00:33:57,970 --> 00:33:59,047
Right here.

605
00:33:59,071 --> 00:34:01,004
♪ Bailey, won't you come home? ♪

606
00:34:01,073 --> 00:34:03,373
♪ Bailey, won't you
come on home? ♪

607
00:34:03,442 --> 00:34:06,242
Well, anyway...

608
00:34:06,311 --> 00:34:08,344
I got a call from the D.A.

609
00:34:08,414 --> 00:34:10,280
right after you left the office.

610
00:34:10,349 --> 00:34:13,249
He's, uh... he's
got another witness.

611
00:34:13,318 --> 00:34:14,417
Who?

612
00:34:14,485 --> 00:34:15,785
Your wife.

613
00:34:15,854 --> 00:34:17,187
My wife?

614
00:34:17,256 --> 00:34:19,923
Yeah, she's going
to speak to motive.

615
00:34:19,992 --> 00:34:21,992
Susan is going to testify?!

616
00:34:22,061 --> 00:34:24,194
Cool it, cool it, cool it.

617
00:34:24,263 --> 00:34:25,695
Uh, Sally?

618
00:34:25,764 --> 00:34:29,866
Uh, bring us... uh... bring us a
couple cups of coffee, sweetheart.

619
00:34:31,736 --> 00:34:34,938
The assistant D.A.
said that she'll testify

620
00:34:35,006 --> 00:34:36,539
that you're so jealous of her,

621
00:34:36,608 --> 00:34:40,376
that when you found her
over at Sam Chandler's place,

622
00:34:40,446 --> 00:34:42,945
you went into a murderous rage.

623
00:34:43,015 --> 00:34:44,814
This is a riot.

624
00:34:44,883 --> 00:34:47,017
It isn't true?

625
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:49,285
Yeah. It's-It's half true.

626
00:34:49,354 --> 00:34:51,021
I am jealous...

627
00:34:51,089 --> 00:34:52,322
because I love her.

628
00:34:52,391 --> 00:34:55,925
So much, in fact, that
I always forgive her.

629
00:34:55,994 --> 00:34:58,627
Which is pretty
stupid, I suppose.

630
00:34:58,697 --> 00:35:00,930
Then you did go
after Sam Chandler?

631
00:35:00,999 --> 00:35:03,867
Yeah, but Sam wasn't
important. I-I... I just wanted

632
00:35:03,935 --> 00:35:06,402
to make sure that Susan
was going to come back.

633
00:35:06,472 --> 00:35:08,070
Then she's lying?

634
00:35:08,140 --> 00:35:09,872
Yeah.

635
00:35:09,942 --> 00:35:11,474
Can you corroborate?

636
00:35:14,245 --> 00:35:16,646
Uh... the maid... Shirley.

637
00:35:16,715 --> 00:35:19,549
Yeah, we could...
we could fly her down.

638
00:35:20,785 --> 00:35:22,297
<i>Detective Cox? Hmm?</i>

639
00:35:22,321 --> 00:35:25,188
Can you identify
this revolver for us?

640
00:35:29,594 --> 00:35:31,494
This is my tag.

641
00:35:31,562 --> 00:35:33,263
That's my mark.

642
00:35:33,331 --> 00:35:36,266
I found this weapon at
the scene of the crime.

643
00:35:36,334 --> 00:35:38,146
It was later determined
to be the gun

644
00:35:38,170 --> 00:35:39,981
that was used to
kill Sam Chandler.

645
00:35:40,005 --> 00:35:42,438
And to whom is
this gun registered?

646
00:35:44,710 --> 00:35:46,910
The defendant, David O'Malley.

647
00:35:46,979 --> 00:35:48,878
Thank you, Detective.

648
00:35:48,947 --> 00:35:51,013
Nothing further.

649
00:35:51,083 --> 00:35:52,782
Mr. Matlock.

650
00:35:52,851 --> 00:35:54,984
No questions, Your Honor.

651
00:35:55,053 --> 00:35:56,753
You may step down.

652
00:35:56,822 --> 00:35:58,721
Call your next witness.

653
00:35:58,790 --> 00:36:02,158
The people call Susan
O'Malley to the stand.

654
00:36:02,227 --> 00:36:06,529
Mrs. O'Malley, how long have you
and David O'Malley been married?

655
00:36:06,598 --> 00:36:07,797
15 years.

656
00:36:07,866 --> 00:36:08,898
And during that time,

657
00:36:08,967 --> 00:36:11,000
did you ever have an
affair with another man?

658
00:36:11,069 --> 00:36:13,036
Yes.

659
00:36:13,105 --> 00:36:14,905
Did your husband know?

660
00:36:14,973 --> 00:36:17,540
I think he suspected
I was having an affair

661
00:36:17,609 --> 00:36:18,942
with Sam Chandler.

662
00:36:19,011 --> 00:36:23,413
Mrs. O'Malley, would you call
your husband a jealous man?

663
00:36:23,482 --> 00:36:25,260
Oh, yes, very. Was he

664
00:36:25,284 --> 00:36:27,350
possessive? Completely.

665
00:36:27,419 --> 00:36:28,897
And did your husband
ever learn about

666
00:36:28,921 --> 00:36:30,220
your affair with Sam Chandler?

667
00:36:30,289 --> 00:36:35,325
Yes. The night
before... Sam was killed,

668
00:36:35,394 --> 00:36:37,059
David found me at Sam's house.

669
00:36:37,129 --> 00:36:38,661
How did he react?

670
00:36:38,730 --> 00:36:40,497
He became violent.

671
00:36:40,565 --> 00:36:41,898
What do you mean "violent"?

672
00:36:41,967 --> 00:36:45,768
He grabbed my face
and squeezed it very hard.

673
00:36:45,837 --> 00:36:47,403
He's a very strong man.

674
00:36:47,472 --> 00:36:49,350
I didn't know what
he was going to do.

675
00:36:49,374 --> 00:36:50,907
And then what happened?

676
00:36:50,976 --> 00:36:52,353
He threatened me.

677
00:36:52,377 --> 00:36:54,556
He made me tell
him where Sam was.

678
00:36:54,580 --> 00:36:55,511
And where was that?

679
00:36:55,581 --> 00:36:57,513
Todd's Grill.

680
00:36:57,583 --> 00:36:59,916
And then what did
your husband do?

681
00:36:59,985 --> 00:37:02,686
He finally let go of me,

682
00:37:02,754 --> 00:37:04,599
and he ran to his
car and took off.

683
00:37:04,623 --> 00:37:07,456
And could you describe
his emotional state

684
00:37:07,525 --> 00:37:09,158
as he left you that evening?

685
00:37:09,228 --> 00:37:12,596
Oh, yes, he was in
one of his jealous rages,

686
00:37:12,664 --> 00:37:15,632
but he was... more angry
than I've ever seen him.

687
00:37:15,701 --> 00:37:16,966
He scared me.

688
00:37:17,035 --> 00:37:19,135
Thank you, Mrs. O'Malley.

689
00:37:19,203 --> 00:37:21,103
No further questions.

690
00:37:21,173 --> 00:37:23,733
Mr. Matlock?

691
00:37:26,711 --> 00:37:29,546
Uh, Mrs. O'Malley,
did the D.A. tell you

692
00:37:29,614 --> 00:37:32,682
that you did not have to
come here and testify today?

693
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:34,184
Yes.

694
00:37:34,252 --> 00:37:37,620
So you, of your own free will,

695
00:37:37,689 --> 00:37:40,089
volunteered to
come here and testify

696
00:37:40,158 --> 00:37:41,424
against David O'Malley?

697
00:37:41,493 --> 00:37:42,425
Yes.

698
00:37:42,494 --> 00:37:45,428
You mad at him?

699
00:37:45,497 --> 00:37:48,698
D-Do you want to see
your husband go to prison?

700
00:37:48,767 --> 00:37:51,134
I believe that David
killed Sam Chandler.

701
00:37:51,202 --> 00:37:52,435
Oh!

702
00:37:52,504 --> 00:37:55,472
So you're here for justice,
and not vengeance?

703
00:37:55,540 --> 00:37:57,407
Oh, yes, that's right.

704
00:37:57,475 --> 00:37:58,741
Uh, Mrs. O'Malley,

705
00:37:58,810 --> 00:38:04,114
isn't it true that you
have had, uh, affairs?

706
00:38:04,182 --> 00:38:05,682
Yes.

707
00:38:05,750 --> 00:38:07,150
And aren't-aren't they often

708
00:38:07,219 --> 00:38:12,288
the act of, um...
an angry person?

709
00:38:12,357 --> 00:38:15,725
Yes, I suppose they can be.

710
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:18,460
But you-you-you've
chosen to testify

711
00:38:18,530 --> 00:38:22,064
against the man who bought
the very dress that you're wearing.

712
00:38:22,134 --> 00:38:26,302
Who provided clothing,
housing for you.

713
00:38:26,371 --> 00:38:30,573
Your every need for the entire
15 years that you were married.

714
00:38:30,642 --> 00:38:32,509
Is this the way you
show your gratitude?

715
00:38:32,577 --> 00:38:35,345
Mr. Matlock, I'm not
a vindictive woman.

716
00:38:35,413 --> 00:38:36,946
You couldn't prove it by me.

717
00:38:37,015 --> 00:38:38,147
Now you-you've testified...

718
00:38:38,216 --> 00:38:41,084
you've testified
that David O'Malley

719
00:38:41,152 --> 00:38:43,186
is a jealous, possessive man.

720
00:38:43,254 --> 00:38:46,322
How-How did he
demonstrate that to you?

721
00:38:46,391 --> 00:38:49,158
Well, he would get furious

722
00:38:49,227 --> 00:38:51,727
if I were just going to go
have lunch with a man.

723
00:38:51,796 --> 00:38:52,828
He would order me

724
00:38:52,898 --> 00:38:54,575
not to go. Hmm.

725
00:38:54,599 --> 00:38:57,367
Well, did you do what he said?

726
00:38:57,436 --> 00:38:58,835
No.

727
00:38:58,904 --> 00:39:03,873
Oh. And did he rave and yell
a-and become very unpleasant?

728
00:39:03,942 --> 00:39:06,142
Yes, he would... he
would scream at me

729
00:39:06,210 --> 00:39:09,112
if I just danced with a
younger man at a club.

730
00:39:09,181 --> 00:39:11,381
Does the name Edward Campbell

731
00:39:11,449 --> 00:39:12,948
mean anything to you?

732
00:39:13,018 --> 00:39:17,787
Well, yes. Edward is a close,
old friend of David's and mine.

733
00:39:17,856 --> 00:39:22,325
He's a closer friend to
you than David, isn't he?

734
00:39:22,394 --> 00:39:23,893
In fact, isn't it true

735
00:39:23,961 --> 00:39:26,028
that you had an affair
with Mr. Campbell

736
00:39:26,097 --> 00:39:27,196
seven years ago?

737
00:39:27,265 --> 00:39:29,465
No. Even though

738
00:39:29,534 --> 00:39:32,535
Mr. Campbell lives in New
York, he does have a telephone.

739
00:39:32,603 --> 00:39:35,471
Surely you must know
that someone from my office

740
00:39:35,540 --> 00:39:36,672
has spoken with him,

741
00:39:36,742 --> 00:39:39,075
don't you?

742
00:39:39,144 --> 00:39:41,945
You're under penalty of perjury.

743
00:39:42,013 --> 00:39:44,413
We had an affair.

744
00:39:44,483 --> 00:39:46,015
And this husband...

745
00:39:46,084 --> 00:39:48,551
this jealous, possessive
man, found out about it,

746
00:39:48,620 --> 00:39:49,552
didn't he?

747
00:39:49,621 --> 00:39:50,553
Yes.

748
00:39:50,622 --> 00:39:53,255
But he didn't rave
and yell or even

749
00:39:53,325 --> 00:39:55,658
go after Mr. Campbell, did he?

750
00:39:55,727 --> 00:39:57,760
No. He forgave you, didn't he?

751
00:39:57,829 --> 00:40:00,396
Yes, yes, that time he
did, but he was always

752
00:40:00,465 --> 00:40:03,866
fighting with me and screaming
at me because of other men.

753
00:40:03,935 --> 00:40:06,368
Come on, Mrs.
O'Malley, if that were true,

754
00:40:06,437 --> 00:40:09,004
your housekeeper
Shirley Lipton would have

755
00:40:09,074 --> 00:40:11,074
heard at least
some of the fights.

756
00:40:11,143 --> 00:40:13,409
Oh, yes, she did.
Shirley heard them.

757
00:40:13,478 --> 00:40:14,410
Shirley Lipton

758
00:40:14,479 --> 00:40:17,146
is prepared to testify

759
00:40:17,215 --> 00:40:20,883
that David O'Malley is not
a jealous, possessive man.

760
00:40:20,952 --> 00:40:22,051
Quite the contrary...

761
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:23,452
he loved you so much,

762
00:40:23,521 --> 00:40:25,655
he forgave your affairs

763
00:40:25,724 --> 00:40:27,656
and indulged your whims.

764
00:40:27,726 --> 00:40:29,258
There were no
fights. There were no

765
00:40:29,327 --> 00:40:31,593
"jealous rages,"
as you call them.

766
00:40:31,662 --> 00:40:34,263
Isn't that a true picture
of David O'Malley?

767
00:40:34,332 --> 00:40:36,899
Oh, you can just trot Shirley
out here on her crutches

768
00:40:36,968 --> 00:40:38,745
and get all the
sympathy you want,

769
00:40:38,769 --> 00:40:40,170
but the fact is, she's lying.

770
00:40:40,238 --> 00:40:42,671
Move to strike the
witness's last statement.

771
00:40:42,741 --> 00:40:44,006
So ordered.

772
00:40:49,947 --> 00:40:51,447
Uh...

773
00:40:51,516 --> 00:40:56,418
Y-Your Honor, may I
have a half-hour recess?

774
00:40:56,488 --> 00:40:59,289
Is everything all
right, Mr. Matlock?

775
00:40:59,357 --> 00:41:01,523
I'm not sure.

776
00:41:02,893 --> 00:41:05,027
Take an hour and
we'll call it lunch.

777
00:41:05,096 --> 00:41:07,608
This court is
adjourned until 1:15.

778
00:41:08,633 --> 00:41:10,532
Stay here, stay here.

779
00:41:18,343 --> 00:41:20,021
<i>Come in, Ms. Lipton.</i>

780
00:41:20,045 --> 00:41:22,323
Come in. Have a seat right here.

781
00:41:22,347 --> 00:41:26,149
That's good. I-I have a...

782
00:41:26,217 --> 00:41:31,754
Good. I have a few
things I need to run through

783
00:41:31,822 --> 00:41:34,335
before we go into the courtroom.

784
00:41:34,359 --> 00:41:36,037
Of course. Now...

785
00:41:36,061 --> 00:41:39,228
how long has it been since
you've seen Mrs. O'Malley?

786
00:41:39,297 --> 00:41:42,131
It was six months
ago when she fired me.

787
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:44,645
Have you talked
to her since then?

788
00:41:44,669 --> 00:41:46,735
Not once.

789
00:41:46,805 --> 00:41:49,939
Ms. Lipton, are you aware

790
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:53,609
that perjury is considered
a serious crime in this state

791
00:41:53,678 --> 00:41:55,144
and is punished severely?

792
00:41:55,213 --> 00:41:57,680
Why are you telling me this?

793
00:41:57,749 --> 00:41:59,760
I want you to also know

794
00:41:59,784 --> 00:42:02,618
that at this very
moment, my investigator

795
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:04,820
is going over your bank records.

796
00:42:04,890 --> 00:42:07,757
Oh.

797
00:42:07,826 --> 00:42:09,425
Is that a problem?

798
00:42:11,796 --> 00:42:13,074
How did Susan

799
00:42:13,098 --> 00:42:16,732
O'Malley know that
you're using crutches?

800
00:42:16,801 --> 00:42:20,303
You only broke your
leg two days ago.

801
00:42:20,372 --> 00:42:23,706
And you say you haven't
spoken with her in months?

802
00:42:23,775 --> 00:42:25,841
Well, maybe David told her.

803
00:42:25,910 --> 00:42:27,342
David told me

804
00:42:27,412 --> 00:42:30,646
he hadn't spoken with her
since the night before the murder.

805
00:42:30,715 --> 00:42:32,948
Somebody's lying.

806
00:42:37,422 --> 00:42:41,324
David O'Malley is
paying you, isn't he?

807
00:42:45,463 --> 00:42:46,862
Yes.

808
00:42:48,399 --> 00:42:50,899
And he is a jealous,
possessive man,

809
00:42:50,969 --> 00:42:55,037
and they did have loud,
ugly fights, didn't they?

810
00:42:55,106 --> 00:42:56,772
Yes.

811
00:42:56,841 --> 00:42:58,121
Ms. Lipton,

812
00:42:58,176 --> 00:43:00,276
give him his money back.

813
00:43:09,320 --> 00:43:11,253
What the hell are you doing?

814
00:43:11,322 --> 00:43:13,356
You had her. Why'd
you let her go?

815
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:14,468
You set me up.

816
00:43:14,492 --> 00:43:15,492
What?

817
00:43:15,526 --> 00:43:17,271
It was a dumb move, David.

818
00:43:17,295 --> 00:43:19,161
I don't know what
you're talking about.

819
00:43:19,230 --> 00:43:20,963
You staged all this.

820
00:43:21,032 --> 00:43:23,365
Somehow you got
Susan on that stand.

821
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:24,767
You paid Shirley to lie.

822
00:43:24,836 --> 00:43:27,636
You filled me with the lies
so I could take Susan apart.

823
00:43:27,705 --> 00:43:28,738
You're crazy.

824
00:43:28,807 --> 00:43:31,007
A lying, cheating wife...

825
00:43:31,075 --> 00:43:32,820
the worst possible witness.

826
00:43:32,844 --> 00:43:34,021
She'd make the D.A.

827
00:43:34,045 --> 00:43:35,645
look desperate.

828
00:43:35,713 --> 00:43:38,548
Discredit his case, make it
look weak and without merit.

829
00:43:38,616 --> 00:43:40,350
And you arranged all that.

830
00:43:40,418 --> 00:43:43,886
You're actually standing
there accusing me of this?

831
00:43:43,955 --> 00:43:46,422
Shirley admitted it.

832
00:43:49,628 --> 00:43:52,228
I know your wife cheated on you,

833
00:43:52,296 --> 00:43:54,075
and I know you're
madder than hell,

834
00:43:54,099 --> 00:43:56,065
and I don't blame you, but...

835
00:43:56,134 --> 00:43:59,635
how in the world did you
get Susan on that stand?

836
00:43:59,704 --> 00:44:01,482
You're not back together again!

837
00:44:01,506 --> 00:44:03,839
I'll tell you how I got
her back on the stand.

838
00:44:03,908 --> 00:44:05,708
By explaining to her that it was

839
00:44:05,776 --> 00:44:08,244
in her best interest
if she wanted a

840
00:44:08,313 --> 00:44:10,979
speedy, lucrative
divorce settlement.

841
00:44:16,621 --> 00:44:19,855
I'll tell you the truth...

842
00:44:19,924 --> 00:44:23,359
I'd love to drop this damn case.

843
00:44:23,428 --> 00:44:25,038
You've lied to me.

844
00:44:25,062 --> 00:44:26,841
You've perverted a system of

845
00:44:26,865 --> 00:44:29,298
justice you're sworn to uphold.

846
00:44:29,367 --> 00:44:31,467
Ben, you want to drop the case,

847
00:44:31,535 --> 00:44:33,447
there's obviously
nothing I can do about it,

848
00:44:33,471 --> 00:44:34,636
but do me a favor...

849
00:44:34,705 --> 00:44:36,772
don't stand here
and try and tell me

850
00:44:36,841 --> 00:44:39,175
that you've won all your
cases by playing it straight.

851
00:44:39,244 --> 00:44:41,443
Because I know
better. I know you.

852
00:44:41,512 --> 00:44:43,257
You're like me. You like to win.

853
00:44:43,281 --> 00:44:46,048
And you will bend the rules.

854
00:44:50,622 --> 00:44:53,256
No.

855
00:44:53,324 --> 00:44:55,324
Not all this.

856
00:45:00,665 --> 00:45:02,431
What are you going to do?

857
00:45:02,500 --> 00:45:04,033
Don't know.

858
00:45:04,102 --> 00:45:05,668
Gonna quit?

859
00:45:05,737 --> 00:45:07,569
Don't know.

860
00:45:10,708 --> 00:45:12,942
Ben Matlock's office.

861
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:16,379
Hmm!

862
00:45:17,615 --> 00:45:18,735
Ben Matlock.

863
00:45:18,783 --> 00:45:20,849
Uh-huh. Yeah, yeah.

864
00:45:20,918 --> 00:45:22,063
Yeah.

865
00:45:22,087 --> 00:45:23,319
Be there in a half hour.

866
00:45:23,388 --> 00:45:25,587
Jack Rinaldi.

867
00:45:56,588 --> 00:45:57,631
Hey, don't

868
00:45:57,655 --> 00:45:58,688
go in there.

869
00:45:59,824 --> 00:46:02,144
He'll spook Jack Rinaldi. Hey!

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
